  "rationale": "`Output::capturing()` sets `capture: Some(Arc<Mutex<Vec<String>>>)` with `quiet: false`. Both `emit` (all non-warning helpers) and `emit_err` (`warn`) push the formatted message into that one buffer under the mutex instead of printing, so warnings and other messages are recorded together in call order (clones share the `Arc`). `captured()` returns a copy of the buffer.\n\nTests: indirect. `symposium-testlib` `TestContext::symposium` runs every CLI invocation of the integration suites (e.g. all 23 tests in `tests/enablement.rs`, which pass) with `Output::capturing()` and returns `captured().join(\"\\n\")`; no test asserts the ordering or warning capture specifically, judged from code.",
  "requirement": "A capturing `Output` MUST record every message, warnings included, in order, instead of printing it."
}
